    "# Day 30: Document Loading and Chunking\n",
    "\n",
    "On Day 29 we wrote the facts **by hand**, one per line. A real company does not have that. It has **documents**: a leave policy, working hours, laptop rules...\n",
    "\n",
    "Today we **load** the company documents with Python and **cut** them into small parts (**chunks**). We learn **all the main ways to cut**, and **how to pick the right one**. On Day 31 the chunks go into Chroma.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🎯 The example we will build\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "company_docs/                          chunks\n",
    "  leave_policy.txt      ──►   leave_policy.txt-0     \"Every employee gets 20 days of paid leave ...\"\n",
    "  working_hours.txt           leave_policy.txt-1     \"To take leave, send a request ...\"\n",
    "  laptop_rules.txt            working_hours.txt-0    \"The office is open from 9 am ...\"\n",
    "  expense_policy.txt          ...\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "No API today. Only Python."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📋 Agenda\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "TOP     Step 5   All documents → chunks     the list for Day 31\n",
    "          ▲\n",
    "        Step 4   How to pick a way          a simple guide\n",
    "          ▲\n",
    "        Step 3   The ways to chunk          fixed, sentence, paragraph, recursive, semantic ...\n",
    "          ▲\n",
    "        Step 2   Why chunk?                 one vector per idea\n",
    "          ▲\n",
    "BOTTOM  Step 1   Load the documents         read the .txt files\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### New words today\n",
    "\n",
    "| Word | Meaning |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **Document** | One file with text, like `leave_policy.txt`. |\n",
    "| **Load** | Read a file into Python. |\n",
    "| **Chunk** | A small part of a document. |\n",
    "| **Chunking** | Cutting documents into chunks. |\n",
    "| **Overlap** | The end of one chunk is repeated at the start of the next one. |\n",
    "| **Metadata** | Extra facts about a chunk: file name, heading, date. |\n",
    "| **Source** | The file a chunk came from. We need it on Day 32 to show where an answer came from. |"
