   "source": [
    "### Way 2: Sliding window (overlap)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Concept:** like fixed-size, but each chunk **shares** some text with the next one. A sentence cut at the end of one chunk is complete in the next.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "size=100, overlap=20:\n",
    "chunk 1:  [0 ............................. 100]\n",
    "chunk 2:                       [80 ............................. 180]\n",
    "                               └─ 20 shared ─┘\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Good:** keeps the context at the edges. **Bad:** more chunks, so more vectors and more cost. A common size is **200–400 tokens** with **20–50% overlap**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use it for:** text with no clear parts, like chat logs or a speech transcript."
   ]
  },
  {
