   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Way 3: Sentence-based chunking\n",
    "\n",
    "**Concept:** cut at the end of every sentence (`.`  `?`  `!`). Each chunk is a complete sentence.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Good:** easy to read, nothing is cut in the middle. **Bad:** sentence length changes a lot, and one sentence may not have enough meaning alone (\"It costs 20 days.\").\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use it for:** translation, summaries, sentiment (tasks that follow the flow of the language)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "- Laptop Rules\n",
      "- Every new employee gets one company laptop on the first day.\n",
      "- You must return it on your last day.\n",
      "- Do not install unknown software on the company laptop.\n",
      "- Ask the IT team first.\n",
      "- If your laptop is lost or stolen, tell the IT team within 24 hours.\n",
      "- The IT team will lock the laptop from far away.\n",
      "- Change your laptop password every 90 days.\n",
      "- Never share your password with anyone.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "def chunk_by_sentence(text):\n",
    "    sentences = re.split(r\"(?<=[.!?])\\s+|\\n\\n\", text.strip())       # cut after . ? ! or at a blank line\n",
    "    return [s for s in sentences if s]\n",
    "\n",
    "laptop = Path(\"company_docs/laptop_rules.txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
    "for chunk in chunk_by_sentence(laptop):\n",
    "    print(\"-\", chunk)"
   ]
  },
