   "source": [
    "### Way 4: Paragraph-based chunking\n",
    "\n",
    "**Concept:** our documents have **one idea per paragraph**, with a **blank line** between paragraphs. We cut at every blank line (`\"\\n\\n\"`).\n",
    "\n",
    "- `strip()` removes spaces and new lines at the start and end.\n",
    "- We skip very short parts (less than 30 characters). These are titles, like *\"Leave Policy\"*.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Good:** one complete idea per chunk. **Bad:** some paragraphs may be very long.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use it for:** documents that already have one idea per paragraph, like policies, FAQs and emails (our company docs)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "- Every employee gets 20 days of paid leave in one year. Unused leave days do not carry over to the next year.\n",
      "- To take leave, send a request to your manager at least 5 days before. The manager must reply within 2 days.\n",
      "- Sick leave is separate from paid leave. An employee gets 10 sick days in one year. After 2 sick days in a row, you must show a doctor note.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def chunk_by_paragraph(text):\n",
    "    parts = [p.strip() for p in text.split(\"\\n\\n\")]     # a blank line = a new paragraph\n",
    "    return [p for p in parts if len(p) > 30]              # skip very short parts, like titles\n",
    "\n",
    "for chunk in chunk_by_paragraph(leave):\n",
    "    print(\"-\", chunk)"
   ]
  },
