   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Way 5: Recursive chunking\n",
    "\n",
    "**Concept:** what if a paragraph is **too long**? Try the **big cut** first (paragraph). If a piece is still too long, try a **smaller cut** (sentence). Keep going until every piece fits the size limit.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "document ──► paragraphs ──► too long? ──► sentences ──► too long? ──► stop\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Good:** keeps the structure and also controls the size. **Bad:** a little more code. It works best on documents with clear structure.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use it for:** manuals, reports, most real documents. This is a very common default."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "12 | Leave Policy\n",
      "108 | Every employee gets 20 days of paid leave in one year. Unused leave days do not carry over to the next year.\n",
      "107 | To take leave, send a request to your manager at least 5 days before. The manager must reply within 2 days.\n",
      "39 | Sick leave is separate from paid leave.\n",
      "42 | An employee gets 10 sick days in one year.\n",
      "56 | After 2 sick days in a row, you must show a doctor note.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def chunk_recursive(text, max_size=120, seps=(r\"\\n\\n\", r\"(?<=[.!?])\\s+\")):\n",
    "    text = text.strip()\n",
    "    if len(text) <= max_size or not seps:          # small enough (or no cuts left): keep it\n",
    "        return [text]\n",
    "    chunks = []\n",
    "    for part in re.split(seps[0], text):           # use the biggest cut first\n",
    "        chunks += chunk_recursive(part, max_size, seps[1:])      # then smaller cuts if needed\n",
    "    return [c for c in chunks if c]\n",
    "\n",
    "for chunk in chunk_recursive(leave, max_size=120):\n",
    "    print(len(chunk), \"|\", chunk)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**✏️ Quick Check:** Use `max_size=60`. Do we get more or fewer chunks than with `max_size=120`?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
