    "### Way 6: Semantic chunking\n",
    "\n",
    "**Concept:** cut where the **meaning changes**. Steps:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Split the text into sentences.\n",
    "2. Make an embedding for each sentence (Day 29).\n",
    "3. Compare each sentence with the one before it (cosine similarity, Day 24).\n",
    "4. If the similarity is **low**, the topic changed: start a **new chunk**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Good:** each chunk is about one idea, very good for search. **Bad:** slower and costs more, because every sentence needs an embedding before we even start.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use it for:** legal or medical documents, where accuracy is more important than speed.\n",
    "\n",
    "Below we use **real embeddings** from OpenRouter (the same code as Day 24 and Day 29). First, the setup:"
   ]
