   "source": [
    "### Way 12: Agentic chunking\n",
    "\n",
    "**Concept:** an **AI agent** looks at the document and at what the user wants to know. It **picks a way** for each part, and can mix ways.\n",
    "\n",
    "*Example:* a hospital report. The agent splits it into *history*, *lab results* and *doctor notes*. It uses semantic chunking on the notes, row chunking on the lab table, and adds the date and doctor ID to every chunk.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Good:** the best fit for each part. **Bad:** the most complex and the most expensive.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use it for:** many different documents that need different treatment.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Late chunking:** a newer idea. We first embed the **whole** document, then cut the embeddings into chunks. Each chunk then keeps the context of the full document."
   ]
