    "**Answer:** AI-driven. Every document goes through an LLM, and an LLM call costs tokens (Day 24). Sentence chunking is just a few lines of Python."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: How to pick a way\n",
    "\n",
    "Ask these questions **in order**:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Does the text have clear parts?** (headings, paragraphs) → **Paragraph** or **Recursive**.\n",
    "2. **No clear parts?** (chat, transcript, story) → **Sliding window**.\n",
    "3. **Is accuracy worth the extra cost?** (legal, medical) → **Semantic**, or **AI-driven** for the most important files.\n",
    "4. **Do small chunks lose context?** → **Hierarchical** (send the parent) or **Contextual** (add the heading).\n",
    "5. **Tables or images inside?** → **Modality-specific**.\n",
    "6. **Many different document types?** → **Agentic**.\n",
    "7. **Just need something fast to start?** → **Fixed-size**.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Your situation | Pick |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Fast and simple | Fixed-size |\n",
    "| Needs a natural flow of language | Sentence |\n",
    "| Clear headings and paragraphs (our company docs) | Paragraph / Recursive |\n",
    "| Long contract with sections | Hierarchical |\n",
    "| Must show the source | Contextual |\n",
    "| Chat log, transcript | Sliding window |\n",
    "| Long report with many subjects | Topic-based / Semantic |\n",
    "| Tables and images | Modality-specific |\n",
    "| Very important, complex files | AI-driven |\n",
    "| Many kinds of files | Agentic |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Rules to remember**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Most real projects start with **Recursive** or **Paragraph**. Change only if the answers are bad.\n",
    "- A chunk is usually **200–400 tokens**. With overlap, use **20–50%**.\n",
    "- **Test with real questions.** The best way is the one that finds the right chunk for your users' questions.\n",
    "- Cost goes up as you move down the table: fixed-size is cheapest, agentic is the most expensive."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**✏️ Quick Check:** What would you pick for each? (a) a 200-page contract with sections and sub-sections, (b) a WhatsApp chat export with no headings, (c) our `company_docs` folder."
   ]
  },
